          "date": "2026-10-27 00:44:11.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-16932 tests: fix sanity-hsm test_251 timeout race",
        "message": "LU-16932 tests: fix sanity-hsm test_251 timeout race\n\nsanity-hsm test_251 set active_request_timeout=1 before archiving, so\nthe coordinator could cancel the request 1-2s after it was STARTED.\nwait_request_state polls about every 1.3s, so it would sometimes see\nthe request go from WAITING straight to CANCELED and fail with\n\"request on FID is not STARTED on mds1\".\n\nShorten active_request_timeout only after the request is STARTED, as\ntest_252 does.  Restore active_request_timeout and loop_period with\nstack_trap, so a failure no longer leaks them into later subtests,\nwhere e.g. test_254b failed because its requests timed out too soon.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-hsm\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Iedb431c23488cece8f4cf503e3adeddd993ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
